newcpu.c: do not trace the STOP spin

STOP does not park the CPU. The run loop keeps re-dispatching the prefetched STOP
opcode until an interrupt reaches m68k_resumestopped(), so the trace hook fired once
every 4 cycles and an idle PAL frame emitted ~35000 entries at a single PC - enough to
swamp the profile and to overrun the 50000-entry ring on its own. Record the
instruction once and skip the spin; the gap to the next entry measures the idle.

Applies to libretro-uae 2b0ed42fe565fb997a0627aaa8f44e0948b527f8 in the order given by
patches/series.txt.

diff --git a/sources/src/newcpu.c b/sources/src/newcpu.c
index 61fc337..e6aff05 100644
--- a/sources/src/newcpu.c
+++ b/sources/src/newcpu.c
@@ -184,6 +184,13 @@ static void adm_cpu_trace_pre(struct regstruct *r) {
 	int adm_i, adm_wlen;
 	uint8_t adm_raw[10];
 	if (!adm_cpu_trace_enabled) return;
+	/* ADM: STOP does not park the CPU. The run loop keeps re-dispatching the prefetched
+	 * STOP opcode, 4 cycles at a time via do_cycles_stop(), until an interrupt reaches
+	 * m68k_resumestopped(). Tracing every spin emits ~35000 entries at one PC for an idle
+	 * PAL frame, which swamps the profile and can overrun the ring on its own. Record the
+	 * instruction once - on the dispatch that sets regs.stopped - and skip the spin; the
+	 * gap to the next entry then measures the idle exactly. */
+	if (regs.stopped) return;
 	adm_wlen = (int)cpudatatbl[r->opcode].length;
 	if (adm_wlen < 1) adm_wlen = 1;
 	if (adm_wlen > 5) adm_wlen = 5;
